      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The diagnosis of delayed rupture of the spleen can be challenging if the history of trauma is remote, or initially missed. Delayed rupture of the spleen can occur in approximately 1% of blunt force injuries to the spleen. We present a difficult case of delayed rupture of the spleen from remote, minor trauma and discuss the literature associated with this injury."},
